---
import Hall from '../layouts/Hall.astro';

const creatorFile = `---
name: Your Name
title: Maker of small strange things   # optional
joined: 2026-07-24
location: Anywhere                     # optional
bio: >
  A sentence or three. Say whatever you like — the Guild does not
  prescribe what a profile should contain.
links:
  - { label: GitHub,  url: https://github.com/yourhandle }
  - { label: Website, url: https://your.site }
  - { label: Bluesky, url: https://bsky.app/profile/you }
---

Anything below the dashes is your page. Markdown. Write as much or as
little as you want.`;

const projectFile = `---
title: Your Thing
kind: game            # or: app
tagline: One line, under 140 characters.
by: [yourhandle]      # matches src/content/creators/yourhandle.md
posted: 2026-07-24
tags: [three-js, roguelike]
cover: ../../assets/your-thing/cover.png    # optional
play:
  bundle: your-thing  # the folder you added under apps/
  aspect: 16 / 9
source: https://github.com/you/your-thing   # optional
license: MIT
---

## What it is

Markdown. Tell people what they are looking at.`;
---

<Hall title="Post a Commission">
  <section class="masthead rise">
    <p class="mark">How things get onto the board</p>
    <h1>Post a Commission</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      There is no sign-up, because there are no accounts. The Guild's roster and
      its board are just files in a public repository — you add yours with a pull
      request, and when it is merged the hall rebuilds itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li class="step sheet">
      <span class="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="step__n">I</span>
      <div>
        <h2>Fork the hall</h2>
        <p>
          Fork <a href="https://github.com/TrustlessMike/vibe-guild">the repository</a>,
          then <code>npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code> to see your changes
          locally before you send them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="step sheet">
      <span class="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="step__n">II</span>
      <div>
        <h2>Claim your arms</h2>
        <p>
          Add <code>src/content/creators/&lt;yourhandle&gt;.md</code>. Your handle is
          the filename, and it is also the seed for your coat of arms — you get a
          unique one automatically, so there is no avatar to upload.
        </p>
        <pre><code>{creatorFile}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="step sheet">
      <span class="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="step__n">III</span>
      <div>
        <h2>Bring the thing itself</h2>
        <p>
          Build your project to static files and commit the output as
          <code>apps/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>, with an <code>index.html</code> at its
          root. It is served from a separate origin and framed with
          <code>allow-scripts</code> and <code>allow-same-origin</code>.
        </p>
        <ul class="rules">
          <li>Keep it under <strong>25&nbsp;MB</strong>. Compress your textures and audio.</li>
          <li>Use <strong>relative paths</strong> — your app is served from a subfolder.</li>
          <li>
            You keep your own <code>localStorage</code> — saves work. You cannot
            reach the Guild's page; the separate origin is what buys you both.
          </li>
          <li>
            Anything needing a server of its own should use <code>play.url</code>
            to embed from where it already lives.
          </li>
          <li>It must be yours to publish, and it must not be hostile to whoever runs it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="step sheet">
      <span class="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="step__n">IV</span>
      <div>
        <h2>Pin it to the board</h2>
        <p>Add <code>src/content/projects/&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>:</p>
        <pre><code>{projectFile}</code></pre>
        <p class="note">
          The schema is checked at build time, so a malformed submission fails
          in CI rather than landing broken on the board. If it builds, it works.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="step sheet">
      <span class="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="step__n">V</span>
      <div>
        <h2>Open the pull request</h2>
        <p>
          That is the whole process. Merged means published. Take it down again
          whenever you like — it is your work, and the Guild claims no part of it.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/TrustlessMike/vibe-guild/fork">Fork and begin</a>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</Hall>

